        {t: "Density of unit cell", e: "Use the formula d = Z*M/(a^3*N_A) to calculate density, molar mass or edge length numerically."},
        {t: "Point defects", e: "Study stoichiometric defects (vacancy, interstitial, Frenkel, Schottky) and non-stoichiometric defects and their effect on density."},
        {t: "Electrical and magnetic properties", e: "Understand how band theory explains conductors, semiconductors and insulators, and classify solids as diamagnetic, paramagnetic, ferromagnetic, etc."}
