        {q: "0.6 g of urea dissolved in 100 g of water produces a depression in freezing point of 0.186°C. Calculate the molar mass of urea. (Kf for water = 1.86 K kg/mol)", a: "ΔTf = Kf * m, where m = (w2*1000)/(M2*w1). 0.186 = 1.86 * (0.6*1000)/(M2*100). 0.186 = 1.86*6/M2 = 11.16/M2. M2 = 11.16/0.186 = 60 g/mol. Final answer: Molar mass of urea = 60 g/mol."},
        {q: "Calculate the osmotic pressure of a solution containing 34.2 g of sucrose (M = 342 g/mol) dissolved in 1 L of solution at 300 K. (R = 0.0821 L atm/mol K)", a: "Moles of sucrose = 34.2/342 = 0.1 mol. Concentration C = 0.1 mol/L. Osmotic pressure π = CRT = 0.1*0.0821*300 = 2.463 atm. Final answer: π ≈ 2.46 atm."}
