        {q: "Calculate the EMF of the cell Zn | Zn2+ || Cu2+ | Cu given E°(Zn2+/Zn) = -0.76 V and E°(Cu2+/Cu) = +0.34 V.", a: "EMF = E°cathode - E°anode = E°(Cu2+/Cu) - E°(Zn2+/Zn) = 0.34 - (-0.76) = 1.10 V. Final answer: EMF of the cell = 1.10 V."},
        {q: "Calculate the quantity of electricity needed to deposit 5.4 g of aluminium from Al2O3 (atomic mass of Al = 27).", a: "Al3+ + 3e- -> Al. Moles of Al = 5.4/27 = 0.2 mol. Moles of electrons required = 3*0.2 = 0.6 mol. Charge Q = n*F = 0.6*96500 = 57900 C. Final answer: Charge required = 57900 C (57.9 kC)."}
